id:                     E408
trigger_tool:           perl|appconfig|conan
phase:                  runtime-consumer|configuration-parse|test-package
error_signature:        .*no such variable|AppConfig.*undefined|lc.*uninitialized

severity:               2
category:               configure, perl, runtime, consumer-test
match_keywords:         Perl AppConfig, no such variable, optional setting, undefined accessor, debug, DEFAULT, stderr
title:                  Register optional AppConfig variables before guarding their values

root_cause:             AppConfig validates accessor names against variables registered before parsing. Calling an unregistered optional accessor emits a no-such-variable diagnostic before a caller-side defined-value guard can run. Registration and value normalization are separate contracts: define the optional variable first, then guard an omitted or undefined value before string operations such as lc.
affected_scope:         Perl applications using AppConfig accessors for optional configuration values, especially daemon or CLI paths that require clean stderr when a setting is omitted.
verification_cmd:       Parse minimal configurations that omit the optional key and set it explicitly, invoke the packaged consumer path, and require rc=0 with the expected stderr oracle; also invoke an unrelated unknown accessor and require the exact no-such-variable diagnostic.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           register-then-normalize-optional-appconfig-value
rec_description:        Add the optional variable to the AppConfig definition with the intended inherited or empty default before read or parse. Keep a separate defined-value guard before lowercase, comparison, interpolation, or other string operations. Verify omitted and explicit-value paths through the packaged runtime, while proving unrelated unknown accessors still produce diagnostics.
rec_command:
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               recipe-patch-and-consumer-test

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      query-appconfig-variable-existence-before-access
fallback_description:   If a shared schema cannot be extended, use an AppConfig-supported existence query before invoking the accessor. Do not suppress diagnostics globally or treat all unknown variables as optional.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       defined\s*\(.*->\w+\(\).*
forbid_1_reason:        A defined-value guard cannot protect an accessor that AppConfig rejects before returning a value.
forbid_1_consequence:   The valid omitted-setting path still writes no-such-variable diagnostics and fails clean-stderr consumers.
forbid_2_pattern:       2>/dev/null|no_warnings|warn.*ignore|stderr.*discard
forbid_2_reason:        Suppressing diagnostics hides genuine unknown configuration names and does not repair the schema contract.
forbid_2_consequence:   Misspelled or unsupported configuration becomes silently accepted and runtime evidence is misleading.

principles:             P005,P010
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

